      description_eng: "The magnificent and extensive building of the French School has undergone successive changes of use, from the private residence of an Egyptian merchant in the 1850s to housing the French School in 1895, run by the Roman Catholic order of the Sisters of St. Joseph, who added the two side wings. It operated as a model school for primary and secondary education until 1983, focusing largely on teaching the French language and instilling French culture in its female students. Eventually, in the late 1970s, it passed into the hands of the Ministry of Education and for some years also housed the School of Architecture of the Technical University of Crete.",
